+/// One bounded write transaction's cumulative physical allocation account.
+///
+/// Every page extent is debited at its rounded buddy size and every file extension at its exact
+/// length before the allocation happens, and nothing is ever refunded, so the account bounds a
+/// transaction's physical growth from above: pages it reuses or frees never lower the charge. A
+/// refusal latches the account, so ignoring one cannot let later work through. `freeze` ends
+/// preparation; after it any request is a publication defect and is refused as `Frozen`.
+pub(crate) struct AllocationAccount {
+    remaining: u64,
+    charged: u64,
+    phase: AllocationPhase,
